> I do think it's important that the jails have fast access to the files
> though. I'm envisioning that they will use notmuch to index the
> data. How will that work? It might be out of scope for this spec, but I
> at least want to think through this.

Each client keeps its own maildir and its own notmuch index. mbsync in
the client pulls the lists mailbox from lab-mail into a maildir in the
agent's home, then "notmuch new" indexes it. After that, every search
and read is local and fast. IMAP is only in the path when new mail is
fetched. This is the same shape as today, where notmuch indexes a
local maildir; only the way the files arrive is different.

The delay is the two polls added together: Fastmail to lab-mail, then
lab-mail to the client. The spec puts the first at one minute and the
acceptance test allows two minutes overall. If that is too slow later,
Dovecot supports IMAP IDLE, so a client can run a watcher such as
goimapnotify and fetch the moment mail arrives. The spec only promises
that lab-mail supports IDLE.

I put the lab-claude side in the spec (mail/isync and mail/msmtp in
its packages), because the acceptance test cannot run without it.

