> How does mbsync handle moves / deletes on the remote IMAP server? I
> think this next part is out of scope for this jail, but I want to keep
> an archive of the mailing list in git.
>
> i.e. I should be able to delete all of emails in fastmail, and not lose
> my email archive.

mbsync decides this per kind of change and per direction. Its Sync
option takes "New" (new messages), "Gone" (messages that disappeared),
and "Flags", each for Pull or Push. A move out of lists/ looks the same
as a delete: the message is gone from the folder.

The spec configures lab-mail to pull new messages only, with nothing
pushed and Expunge None. A message that vanishes from lists/ on
Fastmail stays in lab-mail's maildir, so the local copy only grows.
You can empty lists/ on Fastmail and lose nothing in lab-mail. Clients
pull the same way from lab-mail.

One caveat, as I understand mbsync: it tracks messages by UID. If
lists/ itself is deleted and recreated, its UIDVALIDITY changes and
mbsync stops with an error rather than guessing. Deleting messages
inside the folder is fine; deleting the folder needs an operator.

